	"description": "Cinematic, captioned life of a leafcutter colony (M17): a winged queen glides down, sheds her wings and digs herself in; sealed with her fungus garden she lays her first eggs; her first workers dig up and open the nest; a fragment is cut from a leaf, carried down and planted in the garden, and fungus grows over it; months later one egg is followed through the egg, larva and pupa nurseries to a new worker; majors clear debris off the busy trunk trail while minims ride the fragments and phorid flies dive at the carriers; spent garden and the dead go out to the refuse heaps; at dusk winged gynes and males come up and take off on their nuptial flight. Real-time close-ups, time-lapses and time skips under fades. About 198 s.",
